<setup>
  <selectFromSequence name="pm" from="-1" to="1" step="2"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="c" from="1" to="2" step="1"/>

  <math name="a" simplify>1.3</math>
  <number name="n">4</number>

  <function name="f">$a^($pm*x)</function>
  <derivative name="fP">$f</derivative>
  <derivative name="fPP">$fP</derivative>
  <function name="g">3-$a^($pm*x)</function>
  <derivative name="gP">$g</derivative>
  <derivative name="gPP">$gP</derivative>

  <mathList name="ord1">L T I M R</mathList>
  <mathList name="ord2">L M I T R</mathList>
  <mathList name="ord3">R T I M L</mathList>
  <mathList name="ord4">R M I T L</mathList>

  <mathList name="orderinglist">$ordering</mathList>

</setup>

<p>
  Let <m>f(x)</m> be the function whose graph is shown below.
</p>

<conditionalContent>
  <case condition="$c = 1">
    <graph size="medium" xmin="-1" xmax="4" ymin="-1" ymax="3" showNavigation="false" fixAxes="true">
      $f
      <label fixed anchor="(2,$$f(2)+0.25)"><m>f(x)</m></label>
    </graph>
  </case>
  <case condition="$c = 2">
    <graph size="medium" xmin="-1" xmax="4" ymin="-1" ymax="3" showNavigation="false" fixAxes="true">
      $g
      <label fixed anchor="(2,$$g(2)+0.25)"><m>f(x)</m></label>
    </graph>
  </case>
</conditionalContent>


  <p>
    We are interested in analyzing how <m>L_n</m>, <m>R_n</m>, <m>M_n</m>, and <m>T_n</m> compare to the exact value of the definite integral
    <me>
      \int_0^{3} f(x) \, dx
    </me>
  </p>

<p>
  <ol marker="a.">
    <li>
      <p>
        First, characterize the behavior of <m>f</m> using standard calculus language by completing the sentence below.
      </p>
      <p>
        On the interval <m>0 \lt x \lt 3</m>, <m>f(x)</m> is <choiceInput name="c1" inline>
          <choice>?</choice>
          <choice>increasing</choice>
          <choice>decreasing</choice>
          <choice>constant</choice>
        </choiceInput> and <choiceInput name="c2" inline>
          <choice>?</choice>
          <choice>concave up</choice>
          <choice>concave down</choice>
          <choice>linear</choice>
        </choiceInput>
      </p>
      <p>
        <answer><award><when>
          ($c=1 and $$fP(1) > 0 and $$fPP(1) > 0 and $c1.selectedIndices=2 and $c2.selectedIndices=2)
          or
          ($c=1 and $$fP(1) > 0 and 0 > $$fPP(1) and $c1.selectedIndices=2 and $c2.selectedIndices=3)
          or
          ($c=1 and 0 > $$fP(1) and $$fPP(1) > 0 and $c1.selectedIndices=3 and $c2.selectedIndices=2)
          or
          ($c=1 and 0 > $$fP(1) and 0 > $$fPP(1) and $c1.selectedIndices=3 and $c2.selectedIndices=3)
          or
          ($c=2 and $$gP(1) > 0 and $$gPP(1) > 0 and $c1.selectedIndices=2 and $c2.selectedIndices=2)
          or
          ($c=2 and $$gP(1) > 0 and 0 > $$gPP(1) and $c1.selectedIndices=2 and $c2.selectedIndices=3)
          or
          ($c=2 and 0 > $$gP(1) and $$gPP(1) > 0 and $c1.selectedIndices=3 and $c2.selectedIndices=2)
          or
          ($c=2 and 0 > $$gP(1) and 0 > $$gPP(1) and $c1.selectedIndices=3 and $c2.selectedIndices=3)
        </when></award></answer>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
         Without attempting to compute numerical values for them, let <m>L</m>, <m>R</m>, <m>M</m>, and <m>T</m> represent the results of computing a Left, Right, Midpoint, and Trapezoid Rule approximation to the definite integral <m>\int_0^{3} f(x) \, dx</m>, and let <m>I = \int_0^{3} f(x) \, dx</m> be the exact value of the integral.
      </p>
      <p>
        Order the values of <m>L</m>, <m>R</m>, <m>M</m>, <m>T</m>, and <m>I</m> from least to greatest and enter those letters in the blank provided below, separated by commas.  For instance, if you conclude that
        <me>
          I \lt L \lt R \lt M \lt T
        </me>
        you'd enter <q><m>I, L, R, M, T</m></q>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <mathInput name="ordering" minWidth="100"/>
      </p>
      <p>
        <answer name="ordanswer"><award><when>
          ($c=1 and $pm=1 and $ordering=$ord2)
          or
          ($c=1 and $pm=-1 and $ordering=$ord4)
          or
          ($c=2 and $pm=1 and $ordering=$ord3)
          or
          ($c=2 and $pm=-1 and $ordering=$ord1)
        </when></award></answer>

      </p>
      <feedback condition = "$orderinglist.numComponents != 5 and $ordanswer.justSubmitted">Your answer should be a list containing the letters I, L, R, M, and T entered exactly once in order from least to greatest, separated by commas.</feedback>
    </li>

  </ol>
</p>